==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)]] spawn after 4.67 seconds<sup>140f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Fireworks Gang]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns.
**2 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**1 [[Othom]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be quite painful thanks to its use of Curse (particularly from Haniwanwan), cowing even the strongest of [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] units. However, some of its difficulty can be eased by luring Othom to the base and bursting it down with the likes of [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]. Still, the stage is somewhat luck-based thanks to Fireworks Gang's [[Mini-Surge]]s and Haniwanwan's many random negative effects. Anti-Traitless crowd control from the likes of [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], and (if owned) [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Driller Cat]] remains essential, even with the risk of Curse, alongside backliners that outrange Fireworks Gang's [[Omni Strike]] like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]]. When combined with the aforementioned crowd-controllers, [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] remains a strong option to wear down Fireworks Gang, especially with his immunities to Curse and Surge.

Haniwanwan can be stalled for cash at the beginning, with the Celeboodles providing good supplementary income. However, a [[Battle Items|Rich Cat]] is recommended if one wants a shot at getting all of the Timed Score rewards.

